course: dictionary
lesson: 11858
title: Words that show how something happens
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you how someone does something. Boisterously is one of them: it describes the way an action is done. «The puppies bounced around the garden boisterously.» Puppies do not wander quietly. They tumble and yap, so boisterously means in a noisy, lively, energetic way.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «The party guests shouted and laughed boisterously.» Shouting and laughing are loud, so boisterously must mean noisy and full of fun. Try your meaning in the sentence: "noisy and lively" fits, so you have it.
explain: Boisterous play is rough and full of energy. «The children played boisterously in the playground, so the teacher asked them to calm down.» The teacher's request shows that boisterous play can sometimes be too much. The -ly ending tells you it is an adverb: it describes how the action is done.
fact: Boisterously means in a noisy, lively, energetic way.
fact: «Boisterously» is an adverb, because it tells you how someone does an action, such as «played boisterously».
fact: Boisterous is the adjective, so «a boisterous puppy» describes the puppy itself.
fact: Boisterous fun is rough and full of energy, but it is not always bad.
fact: The word can describe animals, crowds and parties, as in «the crowd cheered boisterously».
exercise: «The puppies tumbled across the lawn boisterously.» What does boisterously mean? | Quietly and slowly | *In a noisy, lively, energetic way | Without any fuss at all | Sadly, with heads down
exercise: «The field mice sang boisterously at the feast.» Which word tells you how the mice sang? | feast | mice | field | *boisterously
exercise: Jayden says boisterously means quiet and still. Is he right? | No, it means slowly and carefully | *No, it means noisy, lively and full of energy | Yes, it means asleep | Yes, it means very quiet
test: «The crowd cheered boisterously when the goal went in.» What does boisterously tell us? | *The way the crowd cheered | The time of day | The goal that was scored | The size of the crowd
test: «After the bell, the boys shoved and wrestled boisterously in the corridor.» Which word means the same kind of thing as boisterously? | sadly | *rowdily | sleepily | quietly
exam: The crowd at the party danced and sang boisterously. Which option best describes how they danced and sang? | *Noisily, with lively energy | Sleepily | Carefully, one at a time | Sadly, in silence
